  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Comprised of photographs, diagrams and text, The Purification records the series of experiments and performance which detail the afterlife of a specimen of local vegetation. The book begins, "Situated at the perimeter of Weeping Beach Tree Park in Queens, New York, was a small pavilion looking on to a stump of the oldest Weeping Beach in America." -- Publisher's web site.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Purification of Fagus sylvatica var pendula was first exhibited for the exhibition 'Crossing the Line' at the Queens Museum of Art, June 24-Oct. 7, 2001.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Edition of six hundred copies .... Sixty copies enclose a laser printed photograph of the crystal jacket and beechnut, signed and numbered by the artist ; the remaining books are numbered sixty-one to six hundred, the first forty of which are artist copies."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
